111 is the port used for the RPC Portmapper service,
This service registers RPC services, such as NFS (Network File System), and provides their dynamic port numbers to clients. Port 111 is primarily used on Unix-like systems (Linux, Solaris) and can pose a security risk if not properly secured, as it reveals running services and can be exploited for DDoS attacks.  

